  "final_answer": "# MacBook Air Price Comparison (Latest Models with M5 Chip)\n\nBased on Apple's website (apple.com/shop/buy-mac/macbook-air), the latest MacBook Air models are powered by the **M5 chip** and come in two sizes:\n\n## 📊 Price Comparison\n\n| Model | Starting Price | Monthly Payment | Difference |\n|-------|---------------|-----------------|------------|\n| **13-inch MacBook Air (M5)** | **$1,299** | $108.25/mo for 12 mo. | — |\n| **15-inch MacBook Air (M5)** | **$1,499** | $124.91/mo for 12 mo. | +$200 |\n\n## ⚙️ Shared Configuration (Base)\n\nBoth models come standard with the **M5 chip** featuring:\n- **10-core CPU, 8-core GPU, 16-core Neural Engine**\n- Upgradable to **10-core CPU, 10-core GPU, 16-core Neural Engine** (for more graphics-intensive tasks)\n\n## 🎨 Customization Options (Both Models)\n\n- **Unified Memory:** 16GB, 24GB, or 32GB\n- **SSD Storage:** 512GB up to 4TB\n- **Power Adapter:** 3 options available\n\n## 🔑 Key Takeaway\n\nThe **15-inch model costs $200 more** than the 13-inch model at base configuration. Both feature the same M5 chip, Liquid Retina display technology, and identical customization options — the price difference is purely for the larger screen size. Apple also offers lease options starting from $24.99/mo (13-inch) or $28.99/mo (15-inch) for 36 months with Apple Upgrade.",
